    "title": "Red Bull Showrun turns downtown Phoenix into high-octane spectacle",
    "text": "The Red Bull Showrun transformed city streets into a high-octane arena. PHOENIX — A stretch of downtown Phoenix turned into a temporary motorsports arena Saturday as the Red Bull Showrun Phoenix brought Formula 1 engines, stunt motorcycles and off-road trucks to East Jefferson Street. Thousands of spectators lined the street as drivers and riders performed high-speed demonstrations, burnouts and drifting runs during the event presented by Red Bull and Ford Motor Company. \"Just seeing something like that going up and down Phoenix streets is kind of crazy, let alone an F1 car in general,\" one spectator said. Former Formula 1 driver Patrick Friesacher piloted the Red Bull RB7 along the usually busy downtown corridor, spinning 360-degree turns and producing clouds of tire smoke as the crowd cheered. Off-road racer Chris Polvoorde drove a Ford F‑150 Raptor Baja Pre‑Runner during demonstration runs, while freestyle motorcyclist Aaron Colton performed stunt riding along the course. Demonstrations also featured the Ford Mustang GT4 and the all-electric Ford F‑150 Lightning SuperTruck. Arizona off-road racer Mia Chapman made her debut at the event in front of a hometown crowd, driving a side-by-side vehicle through drifting runs on the street course. \"I think this is extra special for me because it's my hometown, so a lot of my people are out here, family, friends, locals, I mean, it's just, it's absolutely insane,\" Chapman said. Chapman's run drew among the loudest reactions of the afternoon, with fans recognizing the significance of a local competitor sharing the track with internationally recognized talent. Watch 12News for free You can now watch 12News content anytime, anywhere thanks to the 12+ app! The free 12+ app from 12News lets users stream live events — including daily newscasts like \"Today in AZ\" and \"12 News\" and our daily lifestyle program, \"Arizona Midday\"—on Roku, Apple TV and Amazon Fire TV. 12+ showcases live video throughout the day 